  "Solution": {
    "S": "Let $f(x) = \\sqrt{1+x+x^2} - \\sqrt{1-x+x^2}$.\n\nThen $f(-x) = \\sqrt{1 - x + x^2} - \\sqrt{1 + x + x^2} = -f(x)$.\n\nThus $f(x)$ is an odd function.\n\nFor an odd function, $\\int_{-a}^{a} f(x) \\, dx = 0$.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\\int_{-1}^{1} \\left( \\sqrt{1+x+x^2} - \\sqrt{1-x+x^2} \\right) dx = 0$$\n\nHence the correct option is C: 0."
  },
